media: ov8856: add 2-lane RAW8 3264x2448 and 1632x1224 modes

The driver's only 2-lane full-resolution mode (3280x2464 RAW10) runs the link
at 720 MHz, i.e. 1.44 Gbps/lane. A receiver that stops at 1 Gbps/lane - the
i.MX6 CSI-2 D-PHY among them - cannot program that, so on a two-lane board the
8 MP sensor is stuck at the binned 1640x1232 mode: the whole field of view, but
a quarter of the pixels.

Eight-bit readout costs a fifth of the bits per sample and lets the same frame
travel at half the rate: 3264x2448 fits in the 360 MHz link (720 Mbps/lane)
the binned mode already uses. The sensor supports it - 0x3031 selects the
sample depth - and the register lists for both resolutions are already here as
the 4-lane modes. Converting one to two lanes needs 0x3018 and twice the HTS,
because half the lanes carry half a line in the same time; nothing else in
those lists depends on lane count or sample depth.

Carry those deltas per mode in a second register list written straight after
the mode list, add MEDIA_BUS_FMT_SBGGR8_1X8 with the BGGR Bayer offset the
RAW10 modes of these two resolutions already use, and make the sample depth a
mode property so the pixel rate, h/vblank and exposure ranges derived from it
follow the mode rather than a fixed 10. set_format and enum_frame_size pair a
code with a mode only when their depths agree, so a RAW8 request cannot
misdescribe a RAW10 mode or the other way round.

At 180 Mpx/s the new modes run 15.0 fps and 30.9 fps.

The values are the ones the factory Glowforge firmware programs on this
hardware, which runs both resolutions over two lanes in RAW8 with the same
0x3018/0x3031 and the same HTS/VTS pairs. It reaches them with a different PLL
divider chain (0x0302=0x1e, 0x0303=0x03, 0x030f=0x07, 0x0312=0x05, and
0x4837=0x58) that halves the link again to 180 MHz and the internal SCLK with
it; that is a self-consistent alternative rather than a correction, and it is
recorded here because it is the configuration to fall back to if the D-PHY
does not lock at 720 Mbps/lane on real hardware.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Scott Wiederhold <s.e.wiederhold@gmail.com>

